From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:27:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 204/207] deepseek_v41: resume a rewritten history from a
 prompt checkpoint (TF_DSV41_SESSION_LCP_RESUME)

Session reuse resumes only from a stored entry that strictly prefixes the new prompt. A client that rewrites the
middle of a long history (a dropped image, an edited message, compaction) therefore prefilled from the last entry
before the change, often token 0 (jayleaton/deepseek-v41-tensorfold-spark#80: 216-278 s at ~500K tokens).

A longer entry cannot simply be cut at the divergence: every layer's SWA ring, the ratio-2 carries, the CED stash and
the drafter rings at token N depend on the history, and only a snapshot taken at N holds them. So, behind
TF_DSV41_SESSION_LCP_RESUME=1 (off by default):

- the round planner also snapshots a prompt at every multiple of TF_DSV41_SESSION_LCP_EVERY (default 32768, on the
  16-token grid) before its replay point; the snapshots are ordinary prompt entries of kind 2, sharing the slot's pages;
- the store's anchor_kind policy keeps those checkpoints as recent as their chat (a RAM restore touches them first) and
  drops them on eviction instead of parking them;
- find never resumes inside a run of image positions: a hit there moves back to an entry at or before the image.

Whatever the knob, an admission that loses at least 1,024 tokens of reuse logs
"sessions: slot S: a N-token prompt diverged at token D (stored M); it prefills from P" (sessions/diverge.zig).

Knob off, the planner's pieces and snapshots, the store's policy and every resumed row are unchanged.

Tests (test-dsv41-kv, test-sessions): the issue's repro through the planner, pool, host pages and store (a dropped image
resumes from the checkpoint before it, rows and state equal a fresh prefill; on 7b79ef92d it fails at runtime with
cached 0), a negctl (the longer entry cut at the divergence keeps its own state: rows differ), the knob-off trace equal
to 7b79ef92d's, the knob's parsing, the planner's checkpoint sequence and damaged restart, the image rule, anchor
retention under the RAM budget and drop-not-park, and the divergence numbers.
